  "prompt": "Customer Success wants credit for won-back accounts. For each quarter of 2025 (event_date from 1 January to 31 December 2025) with a reactivation, how many accounts came back and how much MRR they brought, in euros rounded to 2 decimals with ROUND? Each event's event_type names its movement (new, expansion, contraction, churn or reactivation); a reactivation is an account coming back after it churned, never new MRR. Leave out the opening events: they carry the MRR subscriptions already had when the data starts on 1 January 2024. Convert every amount to euros at one fixed rate, that of 31 December 2025: multiply by fx_rates.eur_per_unit for the subscription's currency on 2025-12-31. Count an account once per quarter. Return three columns, in this order: quarter_start (the first day of the quarter), accounts and reactivation_mrr. Return one row for each such quarter. Any row order is fine.",
